# probe.jar — spec 22 class-E proof fixture (§3.3), PRECOMPILED

The boot-smoke fixture jar is a DATA FILE to the smoke: no CI leg needs a
JDK. It rides the InterposeFixture image at `/probe/lib/probe.jar`; the
probe spawns `java -jar` on it (shell-string and array-form) and asserts
the `CLASS-E-EXEC-OK` marker, which only prints when the JVM read the jar
through the interposed surface.

Pinned content (verify after any checkout-level doubt):

    sha256  124bd2d63eab9968722a75d6c71b349c9e4788a486d98b957b545c719f08ab6c

Regeneration (from ProbeJar.java in this directory):

    javac --release 11 ProbeJar.java
    jar cfe probe.jar ProbeJar ProbeJar.class
    java -jar probe.jar    # must print: CLASS-E-EXEC-OK file:/…/probe.jar

`--release 11` keeps the bytecode loadable on every JVM the legs and the
openjdk payload carry (class file 55). Jar metadata (mtimes) is NOT
deterministic: a regenerated jar's sha256 differs — update the pin above
in the same commit, and never regenerate on a leg.
